WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.100
Propene has a carbon to carbon double
bond, and its two ends are different.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.020
Hydrogen bromide adds
across that double bond:

3
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:11.040
hydrogen to one carbon,
bromine to the other.

4
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:16.600
That can happen two ways round,
giving 1-bromopropane or 2-bromopropane.

5
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:17.940
Both are possible.

6
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:21.240
Yet one product wins almost every time.

7
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.890
So why does one product
win almost every time?

8
00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:27.860
In this mission, you'll meet carbocations:

9
00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.820
carbon atoms that carry a positive charge.

10
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:32.860
Then you'll draw curly
arrows for the addition,

11
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:35.800
and predict the products
for other alkenes.

12
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:40.280
Your mission: explain why one
product wins almost every time.